After reviewing analayo-nibbana, shiva-sutras, vatulanatha, and your uploaded essay-visual-engine.zip, I can see the system you are converging on.

The key is that you are building a new way of publishing and experiencing difficult sacred texts, not simply producing illustrated audiobooks.

There are two distinct finished works:

Standard Compilation: the complete text in its proper order, with recitation, faithful translation, recorded explanation and additional commentary. The Śiva Sūtras repository explicitly locks this as the fidelity-first version.

Custom Compilation: the enquiry-based interpretation. The spine is heard at progressively greater depth through Essays 0, A, B and C. The archival voices remain intact, but passages are arranged around the most illuminating questions.

The visual engine should serve both, using the same source data. You should never need to rebuild the visuals manually when a text moves from its complete edition into its custom film.

